---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro'

const title = 'JPEG XL Decoder, Lossless Encoder, and JPEG Transcoder | PureJsImage'
const description =
  'Inspect and decode JPEG XL, try the experimental lossless Modular encoder, and verify exact coefficient-domain JPEG transcoding in a local browser worker.'
const canonical = 'https://purejsimage.com/jpeg-xl/'
const socialImage = 'https://purejsimage.com/assets/jpeg-xl-og.png'
const structuredData = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    {
      '@type': 'WebApplication',
      name: 'PureJsImage JPEG XL Workbench',
      applicationCategory: 'DeveloperApplication',
      browserRequirements: 'A modern browser with JavaScript and Web Workers',
      description,
      url: canonical,
    },
    {
      '@type': 'TechArticle',
      headline: 'JPEG XL decoder, lossless encoder, and exact JPEG transcoder for JavaScript',
      description,
      mainEntityOfPage: canonical,
      author: { '@type': 'Organization', name: 'PureJsImage' },
    },
    {
      '@type': 'BreadcrumbList',
      itemListElement: [
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 1, name: 'PureJsImage', item: 'https://purejsimage.com/' },
        { '@type': 'ListItem', position: 2, name: 'JPEG XL', item: canonical },
      ],
    },
  ],
}
---

<SiteLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} bodyClass="jxl-page" current="jpeg-xl/" openGraph={{ title, description, url: canonical, image: socialImage, imageWidth: 1200, imageHeight: 630, imageAlt: 'Source JPEG converted to JPEG XL with separate pixel-exact and verified byte-exact reconstruction paths' }} twitterCard="summary_large_image">
  <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(structuredData)} />
  <main id="main" class="jxl-shell">
    <header class="jxl-hero">
      <div><p class="eyebrow">JPEG XL</p><h1>Decode JPEG XL and verify exact JPEG transcoding in JavaScript</h1><p class="lede">PureJsImage implements a checked static JPEG XL subset in first-party TypeScript. This workbench runs in a browser worker and keeps local files on your device.</p></div>
      <aside><strong>Local-only processing</strong><span>No selected image is uploaded to an application server.</span></aside>
    </header>

    <section class="jxl-card quick"><h2>Quick answer</h2><p>PureJsImage decodes the documented lossless Modular subset and selected 8-bit single-group XYB VarDCT fixtures. Its experimental effort-1 encoder writes pixel-lossless Modular images from supported sRGB pixels. A separate API transcodes eligible three-component baseline or progressive JPEG coefficients and verifies byte-exact JPEG reconstruction before success.</p><p>These are three different contracts. Pixel-lossless JPEG XL preserves decoded samples, not the original JPEG bytes. Exact JPEG transcode preserves the original JPEG byte stream. Selected VarDCT is decode-only; PureJsImage has no general lossy JPEG XL encoder.</p></section>

    <section class="workbench" aria-labelledby="jxl-workbench-heading">
      <div class="workbench-heading"><div><p class="eyebrow">Interactive workbench</p><h2 id="jxl-workbench-heading">Encode pixels, inspect JPEG XL, or transcode JPEG</h2></div><p id="jxl-status" role="status">Loading a deterministic JPEG sample…</p></div>
      <div class="jxl-grid">
        <aside class="jxl-card controls">
          <h3>Open</h3>
          <button id="jxl-open-jpeg" type="button">Open eligible JPEG sample</button>
          <button id="jxl-open-jxl" type="button">Open reconstructed JPEG XL sample</button>
          <button id="jxl-open-png" type="button">Open pixel-lossless PNG sample</button>
          <label>Local JPEG, JPEG XL, PNG, or TIFF<input id="jxl-file" type="file" accept="image/jpeg,image/jxl,image/png,image/tiff,.jpg,.jpeg,.jxl,.png,.tif,.tiff" /></label>
          <h3>Run</h3>
          <button id="jxl-encode" type="button" disabled>Pixel-lossless encode <span class="badge">Experimental</span></button>
          <label class="check"><input id="jxl-only-if-smaller" type="checkbox" /> Require JPEG XL output to be smaller</label>
          <button id="jxl-transcode" type="button" disabled>Exact JPEG to JPEG XL <span class="badge">Experimental</span></button>
          <button id="jxl-reconstruct" type="button" disabled>Reconstruct original JPEG</button>
          <button id="jxl-reopen" type="button" disabled>Reopen latest JPEG XL</button>
          <button id="jxl-download" type="button" disabled>Download latest output</button>
          <p class="note">Pixel-lossless encode preserves supported decoded samples. The exact JPEG path transfers quantized DCT coefficients and reconstruction metadata without decoding RGB first. The size requirement is off unless you select it.</p>
        </aside>
        <div class="results">
          <article class="jxl-card preview"><h3>Decoded preview</h3><canvas id="jxl-preview" aria-label="Decoded JPEG or JPEG XL preview"></canvas></article>
          <article class="jxl-card"><h3>Result summary</h3><dl id="jxl-summary"><div><dt>Status</dt><dd>Waiting</dd></div></dl></article>
          <details class="jxl-card"><summary>Inspection and execution evidence</summary><pre id="jxl-details">Waiting for local inspection.</pre></details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Use the ordinary pixel pipeline</h2><pre><code>{`import { createImageLibrary } from 'purejsimage'
import { jpegxlCodec } from 'purejsimage/codecs/jpegxl'

const images = createImageLibrary([jpegxlCodec])
const output = await images.open(input)
  .jpegxl({ mode: 'lossless', effort: 1, container: true })
  .toUint8Array()`}</code></pre><p>The encoder currently accepts native gray8, gray16, rgb8, rgb16, rgba8, and rgba16 input. It is experimental because the fixed compression, broader independent decoder, metadata, and sequential-output gates remain open.</p></section>

    <section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Transcode eligible JPEG coefficients</h2><pre><code>{`import {
  transcodeJpegToJpegXl,
  reconstructJpegFromJpegXl,
} from 'purejsimage/jpegxl'

const result = await transcodeJpegToJpegXl(jpegBytes, {
  reconstruction: 'required',
  onlyIfSmaller: false,
})
const originalJpeg = await reconstructJpegFromJpegXl(result.data)`}</code></pre><p>The default policy requires exact reconstruction and verifies every byte before returning. Use <code>reconstruction: 'prefer'</code> with <code>fallback: 'pixel-lossless'</code> only when preserving decoded pixels is acceptable and preserving the original JPEG file is not required.</p></section>

    <section class="jxl-card copy"><h2>Current limits</h2><ul><li>Static images only. Multiple visible frames and animation are unsupported.</li><li>VarDCT support is limited to selected 8-bit single-group XYB fixtures without alpha or orientation extra fields. The decoder materializes the selected full frame, then applies crop and serves bounded rows.</li><li>The exact JPEG path covers the checked three-component 8-bit Huffman baseline and progressive subset. Exif orientation must be absent or 1. ICC must be absent or the exact independently checked sRGB profile. Grayscale, CMYK, YCCK, non-sRGB ICC, and other unsupported JPEG syntax fail explicitly.</li><li>The experimental full-frame Modular encoder accepts full-range sRGB gray or RGB pixels with no alpha or straight alpha. Missing, unspecified, linear, premultiplied, ICC-backed, and other unsupported color semantics are rejected.</li><li>The encoder and transcoder retain bounded full input and output buffers today. Sink-mode transcode does not also return duplicate output bytes.</li><li>No runtime library, native addon, external binary, or automatically selected WebAssembly implementation is used.</li></ul></section>

    <section id="faq" class="jxl-card copy"><h2>FAQ</h2><details><summary>What is JPEG XL?</summary><p>JPEG XL is an image format for lossless and lossy images. It also defines a way to carry JPEG coefficients and reconstruction data.</p></details><details><summary>Can JavaScript decode JXL?</summary><p>Yes. PureJsImage decodes its checked static JPEG XL subset in first-party TypeScript in Node.js and modern browsers.</p></details><details><summary>What does pixel-lossless mean?</summary><p>Pixel-lossless output preserves the supported decoded sample values. It does not promise the same source file bytes or metadata layout.</p></details><details><summary>Can PureJsImage reconstruct the original JPEG byte for byte?</summary><p>Yes, for the documented eligible JPEG subset. Exact mode reconstructs the finished JPEG XL and verifies every byte before it succeeds.</p></details><details><summary>Why can an exact JXL be larger than its source JPEG?</summary><p>The experimental writer prioritizes correct coefficient transfer and reconstruction. Its current coding choices can add more overhead than they remove.</p></details><details><summary>Which JPEG files are currently eligible?</summary><p>Eligible files use the checked three-component 8-bit Huffman baseline or progressive subset, supported marker structure, orientation absent or 1, and no ICC or the checked sRGB ICC.</p></details><details><summary>Are Exif orientation and non-sRGB ICC supported by exact transcode?</summary><p>Non-default Exif orientation and non-sRGB or malformed ICC profiles are rejected because the current JPEG XL codestream writer cannot represent those display semantics correctly.</p></details><details><summary>Does PureJsImage have a general lossy JPEG XL encoder?</summary><p>No. The encoder is a constrained experimental pixel-lossless Modular writer. The selected lossy VarDCT path is decode-only.</p></details><details><summary>Does this work in Node.js and browsers?</summary><p>Yes. The shared codec runs in both. This page performs local work in a browser worker, and Node.js uses the same portable implementation through its platform adapters.</p></details></section>
  </main>
  <script type="module" src="/assets/jpegxl-workbench.js"></script>
</SiteLayout>

<style>
  .jxl-shell{width:min(1180px,calc(100% - 2rem));margin:0 auto;padding:3rem 0 5rem}.jxl-hero{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;align-items:end;gap:2rem;margin-bottom:1.5rem}.jxl-hero h1{font-size:clamp(2.3rem,6vw,4.8rem);line-height:.98;max-width:18ch;margin:.25rem 0 1rem}.lede{font-size:1.15rem;max-width:55rem}.eyebrow{text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.12em;font-weight:800;color:#6f43c0}.jxl-hero aside,.jxl-card{border:1px solid var(--border-color,#cad3d8);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--surface,#fff)}.jxl-hero aside{display:grid;gap:.3rem;max-width:19rem;padding:1rem}.jxl-card{padding:1.1rem}.quick{border-left:6px solid #6f43c0;margin-bottom:2rem}.workbench{margin:2rem 0}.workbench-heading{display:flex;align-items:end;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem}.workbench-heading h2{margin:.2rem 0;font-size:clamp(1.7rem,4vw,2.7rem)}#jxl-status{padding:.7rem 1rem;border-left:4px solid #6f43c0;background:color-mix(in srgb,#6f43c0 8%,transparent);max-width:30rem}.jxl-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(15rem,21rem) minmax(0,1fr);gap:1rem;align-items:start}.controls{display:grid;gap:.75rem;position:sticky;top:1rem}.controls label{display:grid;gap:.35rem;font-weight:650}.controls label.check{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:.55rem;font-size:.86rem}.controls label.check input{width:1.1rem;height:1.1rem;padding:0}.controls button,.controls input{font:inherit;padding:.65rem;border:1px solid var(--border-color,#aab7be);border-radius:.55rem;background:var(--surface,#fff);color:inherit}.controls button:not(:disabled){cursor:pointer}.controls :focus-visible{outline:3px solid #8a5bd2;outline-offset:2px}.badge{display:inline-block;margin-left:.3rem;padding:.08rem .35rem;border-radius:999px;background:#fff0c2;color:#694b00;font-size:.68rem;font-weight:800;text-transform:uppercase}.note{font-size:.82rem;line-height:1.5}.results{display:grid;gap:1rem}.preview canvas{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;max-height:34rem;object-fit:contain;background:repeating-conic-gradient(#e8ecee 0 25%,#f7f8f8 0 50%) 50%/20px 20px}#jxl-summary{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:.65rem}#jxl-summary div{padding:.65rem;background:color-mix(in srgb,#6f43c0 7%,transparent);border-radius:.5rem}#jxl-summary dt{font-size:.72rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:.05em}#jxl-summary dd{margin:.2rem 0 0;font-weight:700;overflow-wrap:anywhere}.jxl-card pre{overflow:auto;max-height:30rem;font-size:.78rem}.copy{margin:1rem 0}.copy li{margin:.45rem 0}@media(max-width:800px){.jxl-hero,.workbench-heading{align-items:start;flex-direction:column}.jxl-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.controls{position:static}}@media(max-width:520px){.jxl-shell{width:calc(100% - 1rem);padding-top:1rem}#jxl-summary{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>
